  "summary_en": "French Ministry of Armed Forces' 2019 AI strategy. It sets guiding principles for controlled, trustworthy defence AI and a roadmap: ministerial ethics committee, data governance, priority areas including robotics and autonomy, coordination cell (CCIAD), R&D investment and international cooperation. France rejects fully autonomous weapons beyond human control.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "France will not develop fully autonomous lethal systems escaping human control; military command responsibility is maintained",
   "Create a permanent ministerial ethics committee on defence emerging technologies in 2019",
   "Risk analysis from design to set 'right level' of trust and robustness; mandatory human validation at some steps",
   "Participate in civil and military standardisation and certification of AI",
   "Create CCIAD within the Defence Innovation Agency; about 430 M€ upstream studies over 2019-2025"
